y:'Cambria Math'\">Conclusions:</span></p><p style=\"margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;font-size:12pt\"><span style=\"font-family:'Cambria Math'\">I. Employees working in the research and development department are not required to attend the office on any day of the week.</span></p><p style=\"margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;font-size:12pt\"><span style=\"font-family:'Cambria Math'\">II. Employees working in departments other than research and development must follow the existing office attendance policy.</span></p>", "hi": ""}, "question_image": "", "quiz_id": "cgl-2026-tier2-mock9-hindi", "solution_heading": "", "solution_image": "", "solution_text": {"en": " <p style=\"margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:14pt;font-size:12pt\"><span style=\"font-weight:bold;font-family:'Cambria Math'\">Solution:</span></p><p style=\"margin-top:14pt;margin-bottom:14pt;font-size:12pt\"><span style=\"font-family:'Cambria Math'\">- </span><span style=\"font-weight:bold;font-family:'Cambria Math'\">Conclusion I does not follow: </span><span style=\"font-family:'Cambria Math'\">The statement allows employees in the research and development department to work from home for a maximum of three days a week. It does not exempt them from office attendance for the entire week. They may also be required to attend important meetings in person.</span></p><p style=\"margin-top:14pt;margin-bottom:14pt;font-size:12pt\"><span style=\"font-family:'Cambria Math'\">- </span><span style=\"font-weight:bold;font-family:'Cambria Math'\">Conclusion II follows: </span><span style=\"font-family:'Cambria Math'\">The statement explicitly states that employees from departments other than research and development must continue to follow the existing office attendance policy. Therefore, this conclusion logically follows.</span></p><p style=\"margin-top:14pt;margin-bottom:0pt;font-size:12pt\"><span style=\"font-weight:bold;font-family:'Cambria Math'\">Hence, only Conclusion II logically follows.</span></p>", "hi": ""}, "sol